<%#
  A labelled menu button: one trigger that names what is inside it, and a panel of related actions.

    render "shared/essentials/menu_button",
      label: "Export", icon: "bi-download", items: [
        {label: "Requests as CSV", path: requests_path(format: :csv), icon: "bi-filetype-csv"},
        {label: "Unfulfilled picklists, PDF", path: …, icon: "bi-printer"}
      ]

  Locals:
    label    required; the visible label, and the accessible name of the trigger
    items    required; see `menu_items`
    icon     optional; a Bootstrap Icons class for the trigger
    variant  optional; defaults to :secondary
    size     optional; defaults to :md, so it lines up with the other page header actions
    align    optional; :end (default) or :start, for which edge the panel hangs from

  This is the page-level counterpart to `row_actions`, which is a kebab because a table row has no
  space for a word. A page header does, and a named menu beats an unnamed one: "Export" says what is
  inside, "More actions" only says that something is. See design.md.

  Counts as **one** action against the page header's limit of three -- design.md's own remedy for a
  fourth button is to collapse the least-used behind a menu.
%>
<%
  variant ||= :secondary
  size ||= :md
  icon ||= nil
  align ||= :end
%>
<%# `popover-fixed-value`: the panel is placed against the viewport and clamped to it. At 320px the
    header's actions wrap, which puts this trigger near the left edge -- and a panel right-aligned
    to a trigger there starts at a negative x. The overlay audit caught it at 320x640. %>
<div class="relative" data-controller="popover" data-popover-fixed-value="true">
  <button type="button"
          class="<%= essentials_button_classes(variant: variant, size: size) %>"
          aria-haspopup="true"
          aria-expanded="false"
          data-popover-target="trigger"
          data-action="click->popover#toggle">
    <% if icon %><i class="<%= icon %>" aria-hidden="true"></i><% end %>
    <%= label %>
    <%# Decorative: the chevron says "this opens", which `aria-haspopup` already tells a screen
        reader, so repeating it in the name would be noise. %>
    <i class="bi-chevron-down text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
  </button>

  <%# `role="menu"` with `role="menuitem"` children, and `popover_controller` implements the
      arrow-key movement that role promises. The overlay audit requires a panel to declare what it
      is. %>
  <div class="absolute <%= align == :start ? "left-0" : "right-0" %> z-30 mt-1 w-64 py-1 <%= EssentialsUiHelper::POPOVER_SURFACE_CLASSES %>"
       hidden
       role="menu"
       data-popover-target="panel">
    <%= render "shared/essentials/menu_items", items: items %>
  </div>
</div>
